The Vauxhall Calibra i V6 was a specific engine variant of the Vauxhall Calibra, produced from 1993 to 1997. As the Calibra ceased production in 1997, there is no "most recent version" in the context of a new car available today. This evaluation is based on the specifications of a late-model Calibra i V6 (circa 1997) compared against benchmarks for vehicles available in today's market (2025). The 'i V6' model featured a 2.5-liter V6 engine, offering more performance than the standard 4-cylinder models but sitting below the turbocharged variant.

